# # /bimei/
#
# BIMei Ontology (ONT) — the canonical Action Statement registry.
# https://w3id.org/bimei/{type}/{slug} (e.g. /bimei/action/conduct) redirects to
# a backing host, which dereferences the IRI (content-negotiates language;
# serves the live head or a pinned ?version=). Identity is language- and
# version-neutral; the register is never in the IRI.
#
# Host split:
#   /bimei/term/{slug}   → https://bimdictionary.com (the BIM Dictionary, the
#                          source of dictionary terms)
#   /bimei/{type}/{slug} → https://ontology.bimexcellence.org (everything else)
# The IRIs themselves never change; only the 302 backing host splits.
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# Bilal Succar — Change Agents
# GitHub username: bsuccar
# Email: bsuccar@changeagents.com.au

RewriteEngine on

# Terms held only by the ontology host stay there, so these IRIs keep
# resolving. Must precede the /bimei/term/* rule.
RewriteRule ^term/(3d-printing-in-constuction|7010-7090|activity-flows|additive-manufacturing|agile-method-in-construction|applications|architecture|bim-excellence|cde|certification|classification-systems|competency-topics|computers-and-peripherals|concurrent-engineering|construction-technique|contracts|cpm|cross-domain-equipment|cross-domain-software|cybernetics|dfma|digital-twins|foundational-traits|framework-model|functions-human|golden-thread|governance|guides|hardware-and-equpment|historical-indicators|indicators|indices|infrabim|infrastructure|insurance|interior-design|iso-19650|kanban|lbms|lean-design|lean-methodology|logistics|machine-learning|mandates|measurements|methods|modelling-specialties|modelling-techniques|operations|organisational-management|plm|plugins|product-data|product-management|protocols|railbim|recycle|refurbish|responsibilities|rfid|robotics|scrum|site-machinery|situational-enablers|standardisation-and-templates|taxonomy-classification)/?$ https://ontology.bimexcellence.org/term/$1 [R=302,L,QSA]

# /bimei/term/* → the BIM Dictionary. Must precede the catch-all. QSA preserves
# the query string (so ?version= pins pass through). 302 (temporary) keeps
# w3id.org/bimei/term/* the permanent, citable identity while the backing host
# stays relocatable.
RewriteRule ^term/(.+)$ https://bimdictionary.com/term/$1 [R=302,L,QSA]

# Bare /bimei/term (with or without trailing slash) also → the BIM Dictionary.
RewriteRule ^term/?$ https://bimdictionary.com/term [R=302,L,QSA]

# Forward every other /bimei/* path to the backing host, preserving the query
# string. 302 keeps w3id.org/bimei/* the permanent, citable identity.
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://ontology.bimexcellence.org/$1 [R=302,L,QSA]
